pgAdmin 4 on FenrirOS
=====================

Installed inert: the service is not enabled, there is NO default account and
no web server site. The data directory is /var/lib/pgadmin4, the log
/var/log/pgadmin4/pgadmin4.log, the settings /usr/lib/pgadmin4/site-packages/
pgadmin4/config_distro.py (override with config_local.py in that directory
or /etc/pgadmin4 as upstream documents; server mode, listening on
127.0.0.1:5050).

First start (creates the administrator account, by your choice of e-mail
and password):

    su -s /bin/sh pgadmin4 -c pgadmin4        # prompts, then serves; Ctrl-C
or put these in /etc/pgadmin4/pgadmin4.env, start the service, then remove
the two lines:

    PGADMIN_SETUP_EMAIL=you@example.org
    PGADMIN_SETUP_PASSWORD=choose-a-long-password

Then:

    dinitctl enable pgadmin4
    open http://127.0.0.1:5050 (put a TLS reverse proxy in front for others)

Backup, Restore and the other tools that run pg_dump/psql need the PostgreSQL
client programs (package postgresql); set their directory in Preferences,
Paths, Binary paths (/usr/bin).
